{
  "id": "heat_traced_pipes___wrapping_factor",
  "title": "Heat Traced Pipes - Wrapping Factor",
  "description": "Wrapping factor when the heat loss from a pipe or tube is higher than the capacity of the heat trace cable. Calculates the \"heat loss - cable output\" ratio to determine if spiral wrapping is needed.",
  "type": "calculator-chart",
  "components": [
    {
      "type": "calculator",
      "id": "wrapping_factor_calculator",
      "content": "Heat Loss to Cable Output Ratio Calculator",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "Qhl",
          "label": "Heat Loss from Insulated Pipe",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "W/m",
          "defaultValue": 150
        },
        {
          "id": "Qt",
          "label": "Heat Output from Heat Trace Cable",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "W/m",
          "defaultValue": 50
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "id": "HR",
          "label": "Heat Loss - Cable Output Ratio (HR)",
          "formula": "inputs.Qhl / inputs.Qt",
          "unit": "",
          "format": "decimal"
        },
        {
          "id": "wrapping_required",
          "label": "Wrapping Required",
          "formula": "inputs.Qhl / inputs.Qt > 1 ? 'Yes' : 'No'",
          "format": "decimal"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chart",
      "id": "wrapping_factor_chart",
      "content": "Heat Loss - Cable Output Ratio Analysis",
      "options": {
        "title": {
          "text": "HR Ratio and Wrapping Requirements",
          "left": "center"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "trigger": "axis"
        },
        "xAxis": {
          "type": "category",
          "data": [
            "HR < 1",
            "HR = 1",
            "HR = 2",
            "HR = 3",
            "HR = 4",
            "HR = 5"
          ]
        },
        "yAxis": {
          "type": "value",
          "name": "HR Ratio"
        },
        "series": [
          {
            "name": "HR Ratio",
            "type": "line",
            "data": [
              0.8,
              1,
              2,
              3,
              4,
              5
            ],
            "smooth": true,
            "itemStyle": {
              "color": "#5470c6"
            },
            "areaStyle": {}
          },
          {
            "name": "Wrapping Threshold",
            "type": "line",
            "data": [
              1,
              1,
              1,
              1,
              1,
              1
            ],
            "lineStyle": {
              "type": "dashed",
              "color": "#ee6666"
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "wrapping_info",
      "content": "## Wrapping Factor Information\n\n**Formula:** HR = Qhl / Qt\n\nWhere:\n- **HR** = Heat loss - cable output ratio\n- **Qhl** = Heat loss from the insulated pipe or tube (W/m)\n- **Qt** = Heat output from the heat trace (W/m)\n\n**Interpretation:**\n- If **HR ≤ 1**: No wrapping needed - single cable is sufficient\n- If **HR > 1**: Spiral wrapping required - pitch distance depends on pipe diameter and HR value\n\n**Example:**\nFor a 4\" pipe with HR = 3, the pitch (distance between spirals) is approximately 5-6 inches (125-150 mm)."
    }
  ]
}